 are there*. It never dims the screen and never stops you tapping anything else. If you are already part of the way there, it picks up from where you are. Tap **Stop** on the card at any time. If it cannot see the next button (you went somewhere else), the card says so and you can go back to the Checkout tab or tap **Stop**. Only one guide runs at a time, it ends by itself after ten minutes, and it ends if someone else signs in. It only offers a guide to screens your role can reach, and to the others it says it could not find anything, just as it does for a screen that does not exist. A window that opens on top of something else, such as the refund window, has no guide, because the ring cannot be drawn above a window. The reply gives you the taps in words instead. A few pages have no guide either, because the button on the way to them cannot be pointed at (an item in the Items list, or Start on a training lesson). The Checkout tab has none, because that is where every guide starts.\n\n### Ask about the shop's figures\nAsk things like *How much is the red Highland Cow, and how many do we have?*, *What is low on stock?*, *How much did we sell today?*, *How many Tadlings did we sell this month?*, *Find order 1042*, *What deals are on right now?*, *Find the customer Priya* or *Which gift cards did we sell this week?* The assistant looks at what is saved on **this till** and answers from that. It does not add anything up itself: sales totals come already added up, the same way the **Reports** page adds them. It tells you plainly when nothing matched.\n\nGood to know:\n- It only knows this till. The sales and refunds it can find are the latest 2000 saved here, and the totals it reports are this till's plus any imported Square history. Other tills are not included, so a total here can be lower than Reports when other tills are selling.\n- A gift card's **remaining balance** is not something it can look up. Use the **Gift cards** screen for that. It can tell you which cards